    "buildOrders": [
      {
        "title": "23-pop Militia full Feudal (Vinch-style)",
        "detail": "A ~23-pop Militia/drush-into-full-feudal build; by then normalize food income. Needs permanent walling to survive fast aggression.",
        "source": "kiritastrich",
        "sourceUrl": "https://t.me/kiritastrich/1432"
      }
    ],
    "buildNote": "Conceptually suited to full-feudal American-civ play (e.g. the 23-pop militia build). The catch in AoE2 is game speed/early aggression, so walling is mandatory. The source channel rates Incas highly — its full guide is titled 'You don't realize how strong the Incas are' and it opens its civ tier list with them.",
    "recommendations": [
      "Open with early Militia pressure, then stabilize food and go full feudal.",
      "Wall aggressively — you need time vs faster/aggressive civs.",
      "Villagers benefit from blacksmith upgrades; Kamayuks anchor mid-game.",
      "Lean on the underrated core — blacksmith-upgraded villagers + Kamayuks + Andean Slingers (anti-archer) is the payoff the source channel highlights.",
      "May 2026 patch (kiritastrich): unit food discount changed to 15/20/25/30% by age (except Kamayuk); cheaper Slingers (50f/25w) and reworked Champs make the infantry + Slinger core far stronger."
    ],
    "strengths": [
      "Villagers benefit from blacksmith upgrades",
      "Houses support +10 pop; free Llama",
      "Strong infantry (Kamayuk) and Andean Slingers"
    ],
    "weaknesses": [
      "No cavalry; no gunpowder",
      "Slow vs early aggression without walling"
    ],
    "timings": [
      {
        "label": "Full Feudal",
        "detail": "23-pop militia opener → wall up → feudal",
        "source": "kiritastrich"
      }
    ]
